ISSUE #5975: 4.20.0 introduce a regression in regexp path parsing (router)
Author: dsi2dldevel
Date: 2024-09-20T12:16:39Z
Labels: bug, awaiting more info
State: closed

[c0]
hello,

I think we ahave spotted a new bug introduced in 4.20.0 during a project express update qualifying new versions.
Versions before 4.20.0 are not affected whatsoever as we have observed.

Versions starting at 4.20.0 fixes a CVE/bug in regexp parser and introduce odd behavior while parsing routes. 

Stated a json route files like so : 
```
[
 { 
"path": "/whatsoever/", 
"impl" : "classA"
}
]
```

The project initializeRoutes middleware cannot set up this route in 4.20.0 and upper while it does work well in lower versions (including 4.19.2)


app being the express instance, the route initializer middleware is like so :

```
InitializeRoutes.getRoutes(link).map((rc) => {
                    app.use('/', rc.router);
})
```

getRoutes returns class instance array that complies to express controller logic :

```
export abstract BaseController {
    router = Router();
    path!: string;
}
```


That king of middleware stuff is working fine up to and including 4.19.2. 
4.20.0 breaks this stuff

How should we fix this to make it work in more recent versions ? 



--- COMMENTS ---
[c1] @wesleytodd 2024-09-20T14:32:11Z:
I am sorry but I do not follow this report. can you give a full working example code and describe the error or behavior you see?
