We have completed a code review early this morning : the way the middleware layer set up controllers counterveine the way newer express version (>=4.20.0) binds route paths to controller instances due to a bug in call to bind method.

The team that reviewed middleware code portion implemented a patch that way :

Every controllers inherits a base class that binds express 'Post' Verbs to the path and instance :

Buggy way to bind the path to the instance that do not work anymore with 4.20.0 and +  :
```
public async InitializePost() {
        this.router.post(this.path, this.processService.bind(this)).bind(**this**);
